Going to the ranger's quest for only the second time and the
first time to meet Scorpius, I was a little apprehensive.
(The first trip was terminated by two centaurs, each with
his own /oDeath.) Well, I either got very lucky or this
quest isn't any harder than the wizard quest.

I located Scorpius by telepathy. The problem, it seemed,
would be those centaurs in the room all attacking me at the
same time while I tried to work out the best way to deal
with a nemesis I had never faced. 

As soon as I opened the door a centaur in the back fired off
a volley of arrows which hit Scorpius. Next thing I know
Scorpius had departed for the stairs. As I retraced my steps
I was able to close and lock a door so I could meet it one
on one. As I entered the doorway, Scorpius took a swipe at
my displaced image. I fired one shot from my /oSleep,
stepped up and whacked it twice with Frost Brand, ho, hum.

This ranger is starting to feel like a combat wombat. Frost
Brand is a much more efficient killing machine than the
Longbow of Diana. With -30 AC there aren't many things I
need to deal with from a distance. 
 
